  "conclusion": {
    "two_gpus_at_equal_env_count": "1.07x - 1.13x across all three modes",
    "why": "throughput scales ~linearly with env count on one GPU (doubling envs gives ~1.9x), so the batch kernel keeps a single 4090 busy well past 16k envs; splitting the same work over two GPUs cannot beat one GPU doing all of it. The ~10% comes from two processes overlapping each other's per-step host and launch gaps.",
    "what_the_second_gpu_is_good_for": "running more envs than one card, not going faster at a fixed count: 32768 envs across two GPUs reaches ~907k env-steps/s versus ~433k at 16384 on one",
    "vram_is_not_the_limit": "~205 KiB/env, so 32768 envs is ~6.4 GiB of a 24 GiB card"
  }
